The 13 Canadian provinces and territories: AB, BC, MB, NB, NL, NT, NS, NU, ON, PE, QC, SK, YT
Was prov12.dom, which held twelve (no NT) until 2026-11-19, when NT was added; renamed for what it holds (NY4I, issue 88).
Each key is its two-letter code. The aliases are the old s50p13.dom list folded in: the call prefixes, NF, LB and LAB for Newfoundland and Labrador, NW for the Northwest Territories, QU and PQ for Quebec.
Included by s50p13.dom. A file that includes it after its own entries keeps its own spelling of any alias both know (the first alias added wins).
No line of this header may hold an equals sign: the reader takes any such line as an entry.

NL = NL, NF, LB, LAB, VO1, VO2, ^Newfoundland and Labrador
NB = NB, VE9
NS = NS, VE1
PE = PE, VY2
QC = QC, QU, PQ, VE2
ON = ON, VE3
MB = MB, MAN, VE4
SK = SK, SAS, VE5
AB = AB, ALT, ALB, VE6
BC = BC, VE7
YT = YT, YU, YK, VY1
NT = NT, NW, VE8
NU = NU, VY0
